     "median": 0.0,
     "count": 0.0,
     "mode": 0.0,
     "single observation": 0.0,
     "unknown": 0.0
    },
    "value": "mean ± SE",
    "said": [
     "To quantify response to road and high lantana, we calculated an index of a species aversion to disturbance as: log $( A _ { 1 } + 1 ) - \\log { ( A _ { 2 } + 1 ) }$ , where $\\mathrm { A } _ { 1 }$ was its pooled abundance in the “undisturbed” habitat (i.e., forest interior/low-lantana) and $\\mathrm { A } _ { 2 }$ was its pooled abundance in the disturbed habitat (i.e., road/high-lantana).",
     "Thus, a positive value of the index indicates an aversion to high-lantana or road, while a negative value indicates a preference for highlantana or road micro-habitats."
    ]
   }
